; Regression (2026-09-24): a second statement added to a BRACELESS body. The
; first line is the whole body, so the parser meets the second where the next
; member should start and cannot go on. It reported `expected '}'` at the
; OPENING brace of the enclosing define — in tscaly's checker thirty thousand
; lines above the edit — because an expected-token error carried the span of
; the construct it belonged to. It carries the token the parse stopped at now:
; line 16, the stray statement. Brace a body of more than one statement.
; xfail: xfail_braceless_body_statement.scaly:16:9: expected '}'
define Calc
{
    function one() returns int
        1

    procedure two() returns int
        print("probe")
        1 + 1

    function three() returns int
        3
}

print("PASS")
